   "source": [
    "# Build SQL Database\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook converts the cleaned user-album interaction dataset into a relational SQLite database for querying user, artist and album activity.\n",
    "\n",
    "The database separates users, artists and albums into individual tables and stores listening behaviour in an interaction table containing user-album listen counts."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "fa238bf4",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 1. Load processed interaction data\n",
    "\n",
    "The cleaned interaction dataset produced in `02_build_interactions.ipynb` is loaded from Parquet. Each row represents one unique user-album interaction with an associated listen count."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 1,
   "id": "45f06abd",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import sqlite3\n",
    "from pathlib import Path\n",
    "\n",
    "import pandas as pd"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "f026b9a7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "processed_path = ( Path(\"..\") / \"..\" / \"data\" / \"processed\" / \"user_album_interactions.parquet\" )\n",
    "\n",
    "interactions = pd.read_parquet(processed_path)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e1b4ac95",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 2. Create database tables\n",
    "\n",
    "To avoid repeating artist and album information across every interaction, the data is separated into relational tables.\n",
    "\n",
    "The database contains:\n",
    "\n",
    "- `users` — unique listener IDs\n",
    "- `artists` — unique artists with generated artist IDs\n",
    "- `albums` — unique albums linked to their artist\n",
    "- `interactions` — user-album interactions and listen counts"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2e5e2cc6",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Artists\n",
    "\n",
    "A unique artist table is created and each artist is assigned an integer `artist_id`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 4,
   "id": "f23f20f7",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "artists = (\n",
    "    interactions[[\"artist_name\"]]\n",
    "    .drop_duplicates()\n",
    "    .sort_values(\"artist_name\")\n",
    "    .reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "artists[\"artist_id\"] = artists.index + 1"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7af59b3e",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Albums\n",
    "\n",
    "Each album is linked to its corresponding artist through `artist_id` and assigned a unique `album_id`."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 5,
   "id": "22a4ed5f",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "albums = (\n",
    "    interactions[\n",
    "        [\"album_key\", \"artist_name\", \"release_name\"]\n",
    "    ]\n",
    "    .drop_duplicates()\n",
    "    .merge(\n",
    "        artists,\n",
    "        on=\"artist_name\",\n",
    "        how=\"left\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "albums = albums[\n",
    "    [\"album_key\", \"artist_id\", \"release_name\"]\n",
    "].copy()\n",
    "\n",
    "albums[\"album_id\"] = range(1, len(albums) + 1)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "dbb4215a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Users\n",
    "\n",
    "The user table contains each unique listener appearing in the cleaned interaction dataset."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 6,
   "id": "45d9b3ed",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "users = (\n",
    "    interactions[[\"user_id\"]]\n",
    "    .drop_duplicates()\n",
    "    .sort_values(\"user_id\")\n",
    "    .reset_index(drop=True)\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "ac37d80a",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Interactions\n",
    "\n",
    "The interaction table links users to albums and stores the number of listens for each user-album pair.\n",
    "\n",
    "Using `album_id` rather than repeating album and artist names keeps the table compact and allows the related information to be retrieved using SQL joins."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 7,
   "id": "dbf1825e",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "interaction_table = (\n",
    "    interactions\n",
    "    .merge(\n",
    "        albums[[\"album_key\", \"album_id\"]],\n",
    "        on=\"album_key\",\n",
    "        how=\"left\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "    [[\"user_id\", \"album_id\", \"listen_count\"]]\n",
    ")"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "8d3463eb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 3. Create the SQLite database\n",
    "\n",
    "The four tables are written to a local SQLite database. SQLite is used because it provides a lightweight relational database that can be queried directly with SQL without requiring a separate database server."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 9,
   "id": "4ccf58d3",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "database_path = ( Path(\"..\") / \"..\" / \"data\" / \"processed\" / \"album_recommender.db\" )\n",
    "\n",
    "with sqlite3.connect(database_path) as conn:\n",
    "    users.to_sql(\n",
    "        \"users\",\n",
    "        conn,\n",
    "        if_exists=\"replace\",\n",
    "        index=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    artists[[\"artist_id\", \"artist_name\"]].to_sql(\n",
    "        \"artists\",\n",
    "        conn,\n",
    "        if_exists=\"replace\",\n",
    "        index=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    albums[\n",
    "        [\"album_id\", \"artist_id\", \"release_name\"]\n",
    "    ].to_sql(\n",
    "        \"albums\",\n",
    "        conn,\n",
    "        if_exists=\"replace\",\n",
    "        index=False\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    interaction_table.to_sql(\n",
    "        \"interactions\",\n",
    "        conn,\n",
    "        if_exists=\"replace\",\n",
    "        index=False\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "05c9a554",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## 4. Add database indexes\n",
    "\n",
    "Indexes are added to the main join and lookup columns to improve query performance when analysing users, albums and artists."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 10,
   "id": "6900d197",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "with sqlite3.connect(database_path) as conn:\n",
    "    conn.execute(\n",
    "        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_interactions_user \"\n",
    "        \"ON interactions(user_id)\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    conn.execute(\n",
    "        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_interactions_album \"\n",
    "        \"ON interactions(album_id)\"\n",
    "    )\n",
    "\n",
    "    conn.execute(\n",
    "        \"CREATE INDEX IF NOT EXISTS idx_albums_artist \"\n",
    "        \"ON albums(artist_id)\"\n",
    "    )"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "865ba7cc",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
